From 3848b156132065f9b182c9e99edd9dffc00f8b4d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aryan Randeriya <aryan.k.randeriya@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 18:51:52 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 13/18] fix(layout): floats and blocks inside inlines resolve
 percentage heights against their block container
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two shapes left `height:100%` at 0 even though the containing block had a
definite height (CSS2 §10.5), which made Amazon's floated tile links 0px tall:

- A float is laid out inside an anonymous float band row or a zero-height
  escape wrapper, so taffy resolved its percentage against that wrapper.
  The post-layout percentage repair now also covers a float reached through
  an anonymous wrapper whose DOM parent is a definite-height block, and a
  parent height given by a length expression without a percentage (e.g.
  calc(clamp(...))) counts as definite.
- A block box inside a plain inline (block-in-inline split) inherited the
  inline's "indefinite" containing-block height during style resolution, so
  its percentage was rewritten to auto. A plain inline or display:contents
  box is never a containing block; it now passes its parent's
  containing-block definiteness through, and the repair looks past such
  boxes to the block container.

Auto-height containing blocks are untouched: the percentage still computes
to auto there.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tm2SNEJ42hMPiZ6cFb8Vih
